From: Lemelson <97357844+Lemelson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:07:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] clock: anchor the monotonic fallback on the pause date
 while paused

When no clock reference exists yet, vlc_clock_monotonic_to_system()
creates the wait_sync_ref fallback at the current wall time. If this
happens while paused (references recreated after a paused seek), the
reference is created at "now" but is shifted again by the whole pause
length on resume, so the elapsed part of the pause is counted twice.

Public clock API probe: pause at t=11 s, fallback reference created at
t=13 s, resume at t=14 s. target+250 ms maps to 16.250 s instead of
14.250 s. In the player, an audio-only WAV seek while paused followed
by resume scheduled the first AUHAL buffer 3.12 s in the future.
Ordinary pause/resume without a seek is not affected.

While the main clock is paused, use the frozen pause date as "now" for
both the PCR delay and the reference date. Playing behaviour, priority
selection and the clock lock are unchanged.

Depends on the previous clock patch (pause date kept across a reset).
Test: redesign/patches/engine/tests/test-clock-pause-reset.sh covers
the late-reference cases (2 failures without this patch) and the
unpaused controls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/clock/clock.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/clock/clock.c b/src/clock/clock.c
index 0c87e54..da0bce2 100644
--- a/src/clock/clock.c
+++ b/src/clock/clock.c
@@ -677,6 +677,11 @@ vlc_clock_monotonic_to_system(vlc_clock_t *clock, struct vlc_clock_context *ctx,
      && ctx == main_clock->context
      && main_clock->first_pcr.system != VLC_TICK_INVALID)
     {
+        /* A reference created during paused buffering must share the pause
+         * origin; Resume will shift it by the elapsed pause exactly once. */
+        if (main_clock->paused)
+            now = main_clock->pause_date;
+
